  "identifier": "metabonet",
  "name": "MetaboNet",
  "alternateName": [
    "MetaboNet: The Largest Publicly Available Consolidated Dataset for Type 1 Diabetes Management"
  ],
  "description": "The largest publicly available consolidated dataset for type 1 diabetes management. Aggregates 21 source datasets into a standardised schema — 3,135 subjects, 1,228 patient-years of overlapping CGM and insulin data total. Public subset (1,895 subjects, 867.4 patient-years) available via free account at metabo-net.org; DUA-restricted subset (1,240 subjects) consolidates OhioT1DM, OpenAPS Commons, T1DEXI, and Tidepool contributions requiring individual data use agreements. Source datasets include AZT1D, BrisT1D, HUPA-UCM, DiaTrend, Loop Observational Study, DCLP3/5, IOBP2, REPLACE-BG, and others. Modalities: CGM readings, insulin pump dosing (basal and bolus), carbohydrate intake, and physical activity. Distributed as Parquet files with open-source processing pipelines for DUA datasets. Addresses fragmentation across T1D benchmarks by providing a common format and scale for training and evaluating glucose prediction and AID algorithms. arXiv 2601.11505, January 2026. Developed by Replica Health and Jaeb Center for Health Research.",
  "url": "https://metabo-net.org/",
  "codeRepository": "https://github.com/replicahealth/metabonet_processor",
